# M4.29.2 observer `is-failed` exit status

Date: 2026-08-28

## Symptom

Sample 1 of the 660-second observation reported a stable Control and unchanged
Candidate, but the observation error trap nevertheless stopped the three
maintenance services.

## Cause

`systemctl is-failed` intentionally returns a non-zero process status when a
unit is healthy. It was evaluated inside a command substitution under an
inherited `ERR` trap, so the healthy result triggered the fail-closed stop in a
subshell even though its text was not `failed`.

## Impact

The services were safely stopped. Control HEAD/tree/refs/tracked bytes/full
inventory and Candidate state passed sample 1 unchanged. No Candidate or
provider path was invoked. The partial observation is not counted toward the
required two complete cycles.

## Resolution

Restart the validated services, begin the 660-second window from zero, and
check the neutral `Result` property with `systemctl show` instead of invoking
`systemctl is-failed`.
